// Refresh the list of updates once a day. Without it, apt's daily timer runs
// and does nothing, and a new install, which has no list at all, cannot tell
// whether security updates are waiting until someone checks by hand.
//
// Sorts after 20auto-upgrades, which Settings writes and unattended-upgrades
// may install with this set to 0. Turning the daily check off is done by
// disabling apt's timers (Welcome's privacy step, Settings), not here, and
// whether updates install by themselves stays with 20auto-upgrades.
APT::Periodic::Update-Package-Lists "1";
